---
description: Flutter customer application engineering rules
globs: ["apps/customer/**/*.dart", "apps/customer/**/pubspec.yaml", "apps/customer/android/**", "apps/customer/ios/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---

Follow `AGENTS.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, and Android/iOS platform docs.

Flutter baseline:
- Flutter + Dart
- Riverpod
- GoRouter
- Dio
- Feature-based modules
- Android minSdk 28, compileSdk 36, targetSdk 36

Rules:
- Keep widgets small and composable for actual reasons, not arbitrary line counts.
- Keep business logic outside presentation widgets.
- Never hardcode provider secrets.
- Do not add Android permissions without product justification.
- Use secure platform storage for sensitive session material.
- Preserve iOS compatibility unless the task explicitly changes platform support.
- Prefer native/system pickers where they reduce permissions.
- Add semantics/accessibility where meaningful.
- Use loading, empty, error, and retry states where network operations exist.
